y mouse ortholog returned by NCBI; one row per human-mouse pair.','from_part1','from_ncbi_datasets'),('challenge','Blah',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,3,NULL,'not found','No current NCBI Gene record matched this input in the selected organism.',NULL,'input_not_resolved','Not queried: Part 1 did not mark this input as resolved; see Resolution_Status and Resolution_Note.','not_requested','not_requested'),('challenge','ENSG00000136997',4609,'MYC','ENSG00000136997',17869,'Myc',10090,'ENSMUSG00000022346','Myc proto-oncogene, bHLH transcription factor',4,'Resolves to the same gene as \'MYC\' (Gene ID 4609).','resolved','Verified the exact Ensembl gene cross-reference.',1,'ortholog_found','Retained every mouse ortholog returned by NCBI; one row per human-mouse pair.','from_part1','from_ncbi_datasets'),('challenge','AADACL2',344752,'AADACL2','ENSG00000197953',639634,'Aadacl2',10090,'ENSMUSG00000091376','arylacetamide deacetylase like 2',5,NULL,'resolved','Resolved from one current symbol/alias search match.',1,'ortholog_found','Retained every mouse ortholog returned by NCBI; one row per human-mouse pair.','from_part1','from_ncbi_datasets'),('challenge','Plet1',349633,'PLET1','ENSG00000188771',76509,'Plet1',10090,'ENSMUSG00000032068','placenta expressed transcript 1',6,NULL,'resolved','Resolved from one current symbol/alias search match.',1,'ortholog_found','Retained every mouse ortholog returned by NCBI; one row per human-mouse pair.','from_part1','from_ncbi_datasets'),('challenge','HYDIN',54768,'HYDIN','ENSG00000157423',244653,'Hydin',10090,'ENSMUSG00000059854','HYDIN, axonemal central pair apparatus protein',7,NULL,'resolved','Resolved from one current symbol/alias search match.',1,'ortholog_found','Retained every mouse ortholog returned by NCBI; one row per human-mouse pair.','from_part1','from_ncbi_datasets'),('challenge','ENSG00000261846',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,8,NULL,'not found','No current NCBI Gene record matched this input in the selected organism.',NULL,'input_not_resolved','Not queried: Part 1 did not mark this input as resolved; see Resolution_Status and Resolution_Note.','not_requested','not_requested'),('challenge','XIST',7503,'XIST','ENSG00000229807',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,9,NULL,'resolved','Selected the unique exact official-symbol match.',0,'no_mouse_ortholog_returned','NCBI successfully returned no mouse ortholog for this human Gene ID.','from_part1','not_requested'),('challenge','MALAT1',378938,'MALAT1','ENSG00000251562',72289,'Malat1',10090,'ENSMUSG00000092341','metastasis associated lung adenocarcinoma transcript 1 (non-coding RNA)',10,NULL,'resolved','Resolved from one current symbol/alias search match.',1,'ortholog_found','Retained every mouse ortholog returned by NCBI; one row per human-mouse pair.','from_part1','from_ncbi_datasets');
INSERT INTO `p3_pair_summary` VALUES ('development',1,'BRCA1',672,'BRCA1',12189,'Brca1','ortholog_found','reviewed_found','reviewed_found','retrieved','retrieved','annotation_overlap_only','comparable',NULL,'[\"P38398\"]','[\"Breast cancer type 1 susceptibility protein\"]','[\"1: Evidence at protein level\"]','[\"E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase that specifically mediates the formation of \'Lys-6\'-linked polyubiquitin chains and plays a central role in DNA repair by facilitating cellular responses to DNA damage (PubMed:10500182, PubMed:12887909, PubMed:12890688, PubMed:14976165, PubMed:16818604, PubMed:17525340, PubMed:19261748). It is unclear whether it also mediates the formation of other types of polyubiquitin chains (PubMed:12890688). The BRCA1-BARD1 heterodimer coordinates a diverse range of cellular pathways such as DNA damage repair, ubiquitination and transcriptional regulation to maintain genomic stability (PubMed:12890688, PubMed:14976165, PubMed:20351172). Regulates centrosomal microtubule nucleation (PubMed:18056443). Required for appropriate cell cycle arrests after ionizing irradiation in both the S-phase and the G2 phase of the cell cycle (PubMed:10724175, PubMed:11836499, PubMed:12183412, PubMed:19261748). Required for FANCD2 targeting to sites of DNA damage (PubMed:12887909). Inhibits lipid synthesis by binding to inactive phosphorylated ACACA and preventing its dephosphorylation (PubMed:16326698). Contributes to homologous recombination repair (HRR) via its direct interaction with PALB2, fine-tunes recombinational repair partly through its modulatory role in the PALB2-dependent loading of BRCA2-RAD51 repair machinery at DNA breaks (PubMed:19369211). Component of the BRCA1-RBBP8 complex which regulates CHEK1 activation and controls cell cycle G2/M checkpoints on DNA damage via BRCA1-mediated ubiquitination of RBBP8 (PubMed:16818604). Acts as a transcriptional activator (PubMed:20160719)\"]','[\"Chromosome\",\"Cytoplasm\",\"Nucleus\"]','[\"MF: DNA binding (GO:0003677)\",\"MF: RNA binding (GO:0003723)\",\"MF: RNA polymerase binding (GO:0070063)\",\"MF: damaged DNA binding (GO:0003684)\",\"MF: enzyme binding (GO:0019899)\",\"MF: histone H2AK127 ubiquitin ligase activity (GO:0140863)\",\"MF: histone H2AK129 ubiquitin ligase activity (GO:0140864)\",\"MF: identical protein binding (GO:0042802)\",\"MF: p53 binding (GO:0002039)\",\"MF: transcription cis-regulatory region binding (GO:0000976)\",\"MF: transcription coactivator activity (GO:0003713)\",\"MF: tubulin binding (GO:0015631)\",\"MF: ubiquitin protein ligase activity (GO:0061630)\",\"MF: ubiquitin protein ligase binding (GO:0031625)\",\"MF: ubiquitin-modified histone reader activity (GO:0061649)\",\"MF: ubiquitin-protein transferase activity (GO:0004842)\",\"MF: zinc ion binding (GO:0008270)\",\"BP: DNA damage response (GO:0006974)\",\"BP: DNA damage tolerance (GO:0006301)\",\"BP: DNA repair (GO:0006281)\",\"BP: DNA strand resection involved in replication fork processing (GO:0110025)\",\"BP: cellular response to indole-3-methanol (GO:0071681)\",\"BP: cellular response to ionizing radiation (GO:0071479)\",\"BP: cellular response to tumor necrosis factor (GO:0071356)\",\"BP: chromatin remodeling (GO:0006338)\",\"BP: chromosome segregation (GO:0007059)\",\"BP: double-strand break repair (GO:0006302)\",\"BP: double-strand break repair via homologous recombination (GO:0000724)\",\"BP: homologous recombination (GO:0035825)\",\"BP: intrinsic apoptotic signaling pathway in response to DNA damage (GO:0008630)\",\"BP: mitotic G2 DNA damage checkpoint signaling (GO:0007095)\",\"BP: mitotic G2/M transition checkpoint (GO:0044818)\",\"BP: negative regulation of DNA-templated transcription (GO:0045892)\",\"BP: negative regulation of cell cycle (GO:0045786)\",\"BP: negative regulation of cell growth (GO:0030308)\",\"BP: negative regulation of centriole replication (GO:0046600)\",\"BP: negative regulation of extrinsic apoptotic signaling pathway via death domain receptors (GO:1902042)\",\"BP: negative regulation of fatty acid biosynthetic process (GO:0045717)\",\"BP: negative regulation of gene expression via chromosomal CpG island methylation (GO:0044027)\",\"BP: negative regulation of intracellular estrogen receptor signaling pathway (GO:0033147)\",\"BP: negative regulation of reactive oxygen species metabolic process (GO:2000378)\",\"BP: positive regulation of DNA repair (GO:0045739)\",\"BP: positive regulation of DNA-templated transcription (GO:0045893)\",\"BP: positive regulation of angiogenesis (GO:0045766)\",\"BP: positive regulation of gene expression (GO:0010628)\",\"BP: positive regulation of transcription by RNA polymerase II (GO:0045944)\",\"BP: positive regulation of vascular endothelial growth factor production (GO:0010575)\",\"BP: protein K6-linked ubiquitination (GO:0085020)\",\"BP: protein autoubiquitination (GO:0051865)\",\"BP: protein ubiquitination (GO:0016567)\",\"BP: regulation of DNA damage checkpoint (GO:2000001)\",\"BP: regulation of DNA repair (GO:0006282)\",\"BP: regulation of cell cycle (GO:0051726)\",\"BP: regulation of transcription by RNA polymerase II (GO:0006357)\",\"BP: response to ionizing radiation (GO:0010212)\",\"CC: BRCA1-A complex (GO:0070531)\",\"CC: BRCA1-B complex (GO:0070532)\",\"CC: BRCA1-BARD1 complex (GO:0031436)\",\"CC: BRCA1-C complex (GO:0070533)\",\"CC: DNA repair complex (GO:1990391)\",\"CC: chromosome (GO:0005694)\",\"CC: condensed nuclear chromosome (GO:0000794)\",\"CC: cytoplasm (GO:0005737)\",\"CC: gamma-tubulin ring complex (GO:0000931)\",\"CC: lateral element (GO:0000800)\",\"CC: nuclear body (GO:0016604)\",\"CC: nuclear ubiquitin ligase complex (GO:0000152)\",\"CC: nucleoplasm (GO:0005654)\",\"CC: nucleus (GO:0005634)\",\"CC: plasma membrane (GO:0005886)\",\"CC: protein-containing complex (GO:0032991)\",\"CC: ribonucleoprotein complex (GO:1990904)\",\"CC: ubiquitin ligase complex (GO:0000151)\"]','[\"P48754\"]','[\"Breast cancer type 1 susceptibility protein homolog\"]','[\"1: Evidence at protein level\"]','[\"E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase that specifically mediates the formation of \'Lys-6\'-linked polyubiquitin chains and plays a central role in DNA repair by facilitating cellular responses to DNA damage. It is unclear whether it also mediates the formation of other types of polyubiquitin chains. The BRCA1-BARD1 heterodimer coordinates a diverse range of cellular pathways such as DNA damage repair, ubiquitination and transcriptional regulation to maintain genomic stability. Regulates centrosomal microtubule nucleation. Required for appropriate cell cycle arrests after ionizing irradiation in both the S-phase and the G2 phase of the cell cycle. Required for FANCD2 targeting to sites of DNA damage. Inhibits lipid synthesis by binding to inactive phosphorylated ACACA and preventing its dephosphorylation. Contributes to homologous recombination repair (HRR) via its direct interaction with PALB2, fine-tunes recombinational repair partly through its modulatory role in the PALB2-dependent loading of BRCA2-RAD51 repair machinery at DNA breaks. Component of the BRCA1-RBBP8 complex which regulates CHEK1 activation and controls cell cycle G2/M checkpoints on DNA damage via BRCA1-mediated ubiquitination of RBBP8. Acts as a transcriptional activator\"]','[\"Chromosome\",\"Cytoplasm\",\"Nucleus\"]','[\"MF: RNA binding (GO:0003723)\",\"MF: RNA polymerase binding (GO:0070063)\",\"MF: chromatin binding (GO:0003682)\",\"MF: damaged DNA binding (GO:0003684)\",\"MF: enzyme binding (GO:0019899)\",\"MF: identical protein binding (GO:0042802)\",\"MF: p53 binding (GO:0002039)\",\"MF: transcription cis-regulatory region binding (GO:0000976)\",\"MF: transcription coactivator activity (GO:0003713)\",\"MF: ubiquitin protein ligase activity (GO:0061630)\",\"MF: ubiquitin protein ligase binding (GO:0031625)\",\"MF: ubiquitin-protein transferase activity (GO:0004842)\",\"MF: zinc ion binding (GO:0008270)\",\"BP: DNA damage response (GO:0006974)\",\"BP: DNA damage tolerance 