issue_id\":\"UBERON:0005343\",\"tissue_name\":\"cortical plate\",\"human_score\":52.32,\"human_quality\":\"gold\",\"human_fdr\":\"1.99e-5\",\"mouse_score\":60.52,\"mouse_quality\":\"gold\",\"mouse_fdr\":\"0.007\"},{\"tissue_id\":\"UBERON:0001954\",\"tissue_name\":\"Ammon\'s horn\",\"human_score\":63.02,\"human_quality\":\"gold\",\"human_fdr\":\"3.41e-7\",\"mouse_score\":49.78,\"mouse_quality\":\"silver\",\"mouse_fdr\":\"0.048\"},{\"tissue_id\":\"UBERON:0002436\",\"tissue_name\":\"primary visual cortex\",\"human_score\":62.03,\"human_quality\":\"gold\",\"human_fdr\":\"8.63e-7\",\"mouse_score\":49.08,\"mouse_quality\":\"silver\",\"mouse_fdr\":\"0.044\"},{\"tissue_id\":\"UBERON:0002661\",\"tissue_name\":\"superior frontal gyrus\",\"human_score\":52.61,\"human_quality\":\"gold\",\"human_fdr\":\"1.35e-5\",\"mouse_score\":56.11,\"mouse_quality\":\"gold\",\"mouse_fdr\":\"0.004\"},{\"tissue_id\":\"UBERON:0002167\",\"tissue_name\":\"right lung\",\"human_score\":66.78,\"human_quality\":\"gold\",\"human_fdr\":\"1.13e-6\",\"mouse_score\":40.68,\"mouse_quality\":\"silver\",\"mouse_fdr\":\"0.031\"}]',0.7631578947368421,0.7857142857142857),('development',2,'BRCA2',675,'BRCA2',12190,'Brca2','ortholog_found','reviewed_found','reviewed_found','retrieved','retrieved','annotation_overlap_only','comparable',NULL,'[\"P51587\"]','[\"Breast cancer type 2 susceptibility protein\"]','[\"1: Evidence at protein level\"]','[\"Tumor suppressor protein that maintains genome stability primarily by repairing damaged DNA through homologous recombination (HR) (PubMed:11239456, PubMed:12442171, PubMed:15115758, PubMed:15199141, PubMed:15671039, PubMed:15937124, PubMed:17515903, PubMed:17515904, PubMed:18317453, PubMed:19303847, PubMed:20729832, PubMed:20729858, PubMed:20729859, PubMed:21719596, PubMed:27941124, PubMed:37499663, PubMed:37515771). Facilitates the repair of double-strand breaks (DSBs) by binding and mediating the loading of the RAD51 protein onto single-stranded DNA (ssDNA), thereby promoting the activity of RAD51, which catalyzes DNA strand exchange (PubMed:11239456, PubMed:12442171, PubMed:15937124, PubMed:17515903, PubMed:17515904, PubMed:18317453, PubMed:19303847, PubMed:20729832, PubMed:20729858, PubMed:20729859, PubMed:27941124, PubMed:37499663). BRCA2 nucleates and stabilizes RAD51 on ssDNA directly and delivers RAD51 to ssDNA-double-stranded DNA (dsDNA) junctions by sliding along dsDNA backbone (PubMed:12442171, PubMed:19303847, PubMed:37499663). RAD51 targeting to ssDNA promotes removal of replication protein-A (RPA) from ssDNA and stabilization of RAD51-ssDNA filaments by blocking ATP hydrolysis (PubMed:20729859). May play a role in the extension step after strand invasion at replication-dependent DNA double-strand breaks; together with PALB2 is involved in both POLH localization at collapsed replication forks and DNA polymerization activity (PubMed:24485656). Required to prevent R-loop-associated DNA damage and thus transcription-associated genomic instability (PubMed:24896180). Silencing of BRCA2 promotes R-loop accumulation at actively transcribed genes in replicating and non-replicating cells, suggesting that BRCA2 mediates the control of R-loop associated genomic instability, independently of its known role in homologous recombination (PubMed:24896180). Also promotes RAD51 loading to telomeric regions, facilitating telomere replication and capping (PubMed:21076401). Also required for homologous recombination during meiosis by promoting the recruitment of RAD51 and DMC1 recombinases to meiotic DSB sites, enabling proper chromosome pairing and crossing over (PubMed:26976601). Also promotes homologous recombination by inactivating the FIGNL1-FIRRM complex to protect RAD51 filament from premature disassembly (PubMed:37515771). Together with NPM1, may also regulate centrosome duplication (PubMed:21084279)\"]','[\"Chromosome\",\"Chromosome, telomere\",\"Cytoplasm, cytoskeleton, microtubule organizing center, centrosome\",\"Nucleus\"]','[\"MF: double-stranded DNA binding (GO:0003690)\",\"MF: gamma-tubulin binding (GO:0043015)\",\"MF: identical protein binding (GO:0042802)\",\"MF: molecular function inhibitor activity (GO:0140678)\",\"MF: protease binding (GO:0002020)\",\"MF: protein-macromolecule adaptor activity (GO:0030674)\",\"MF: single-stranded DNA binding (GO:0003697)\",\"BP: DNA damage response (GO:0006974)\",\"BP: DNA recombinase assembly (GO:0000730)\",\"BP: cellular response to ionizing radiation (GO:0071479)\",\"BP: centrosome duplication (GO:0051298)\",\"BP: double-strand break repair (GO:0006302)\",\"BP: double-strand break repair involved in meiotic recombination (GO:1990918)\",\"BP: double-strand break repair via homologous recombination (GO:0000724)\",\"BP: establishment of protein localization to telomere (GO:0070200)\",\"BP: male meiosis I (GO:0007141)\",\"BP: mitotic recombination-dependent replication fork processing (GO:1990426)\",\"BP: negative regulation of mammary gland epithelial cell proliferation (GO:0033600)\",\"BP: nucleotide-excision repair (GO:0006289)\",\"BP: positive regulation of DNA-templated transcription (GO:0045893)\",\"BP: regulation of DNA damage checkpoint (GO:2000001)\",\"BP: regulation of DNA-templated transcription (GO:0006355)\",\"BP: telomere maintenance via recombination (GO:0000722)\",\"CC: BRCA2-MAGE-D1 complex (GO:0033593)\",\"CC: DNA repair complex (GO:1990391)\",\"CC: centrosome (GO:0005813)\",\"CC: chromosome, telomeric region (GO:0000781)\",\"CC: cytosol (GO:0005829)\",\"CC: lateral element (GO:0000800)\",\"CC: nuclear ubiquitin ligase complex (GO:0000152)\",\"CC: nucleoplasm (GO:0005654)\",\"CC: nucleus (GO:0005634)\",\"CC: protein-containing complex (GO:0032991)\",\"CC: secretory granule (GO:0030141)\",\"CC: site of double-strand break (GO:0035861)\"]','[\"P97929\"]','[\"Breast cancer type 2 susceptibility protein homolog\"]','[\"1: Evidence at protein level\"]','[\"Tumor suppressor protein that maintains genome stability primarily by repairing damaged DNA through homologous recombination (HR) (PubMed:9126738). Facilitates the repair of double-strand breaks (DSBs) by binding and mediating the loading of the RAD51 protein onto single-stranded DNA (ssDNA), thereby promoting the activity of RAD51, which catalyzes DNA strand exchange (By similarity). BRCA2 nucleates and stabilizes RAD51 on ssDNA directly and delivers RAD51 to ssDNA-double-stranded DNA (dsDNA) junctions by sliding along dsDNA backbone (By similarity). RAD51 targeting to ssDNA promotes removal of replication protein-A (RPA) from ssDNA and stabilization of RAD51-ssDNA filaments by blocking ATP hydrolysis (By similarity). May play a role in the extension step after strand invasion at replication-dependent DNA double-strand breaks; together with PALB2 is involved in both POLH localization at collapsed replication forks and DNA polymerization activity (By similarity). Required to prevent R-loop-associated DNA damage and thus transcription-associated genomic instability (By similarity). Silencing of BRCA2 promotes R-loop accumulation at actively transcribed genes in replicating and non-replicating cells, suggesting that BRCA2 mediates the control of R-loop associated genomic instability, independently of its known role in homologous recombination (By similarity). Also promotes RAD51 loading to telomeric regions, facilitating telomere replication and capping (By similarity). Also required for homologous recombination during meiosis by promoting the recruitment of RAD51 and DMC1 recombinases to meiotic DSB sites, enabling proper chromosome pairing and crossing over (By similarity). Also promotes homologous recombination by inactivating the FIGNL1-FIRRM complex to protect RAD51 filament from premature disassembly (By similarity). Together with NPM1, may also regulate centrosome duplication (By similarity)\"]','[\"Chromosome\",\"Chromosome, telomere\",\"Cytoplasm, cytoskeleton, microtubule organizing center, centrosome\",\"Nucleus\"]','[\"MF: double-stranded DNA binding (GO:0003690)\",\"MF: gamma-tubulin binding (GO:0043015)\",\"MF: histone H3 acetyltransferase activity (GO:0010484)\",\"MF: histone H4 acetyltransferase activity (GO:0010485)\",\"MF: identical protein binding (GO:0042802)\",\"MF: molecular function inhibitor activity (GO:0140678)\",\"MF: protease binding (GO:0002020)\",\"MF: protein-macromolecule adaptor activity (GO:0030674)\",\"MF: single-stranded DNA binding (GO:0003697)\",\"BP: DNA damage response (GO:0006974)\",\"BP: DNA damage response, signal transduction by p53 class mediator (GO:0030330)\",\"BP: DNA recombinase assembly (GO:0000730)\",\"BP: DNA recombination (GO:0006310)\",\"BP: brain development (GO:0007420)\",\"BP: cell population proliferation (GO:0008283)\",\"BP: cellular response to ionizing radiation (GO:0071479)\",\"BP: cellular senescence (GO:0090398)\",\"BP: centrosome duplication (GO:0051298)\",\"BP: chordate embryonic development (GO:0043009)\",\"BP: chromosome organization (GO:0051276)\",\"BP: double-strand break repair (GO:0006302)\",\"BP: double-strand break repair involved in meiotic recombination (GO:1990918)\",\"BP: double-strand break repair via homologous recombination (GO:0000724)\",\"BP: establishment of protein localization to telomere (GO:0070200)\",\"BP: female gonad development (GO:0008585)\",\"BP: hemopoiesis (GO:0030097)\",\"BP: homologous chromosome orientation in meiotic metaphase I (GO:0031619)\",\"BP: inner cell mass cell proliferation (GO:0001833)\",\"BP: intrinsic apoptotic signaling pathway in response to DNA damage (GO:0008630)\",\"BP: intrinsic apoptotic signaling pathway in response to DNA damage by p53 class mediator (GO:0042771)\",\"BP: male meiosis I (GO:0007141)\",\"BP: mammary gland development (GO:0030879)\",\"BP: mitotic recombination-dependent replication fork processing (GO:1990426)\",\"BP: multicellular organism growth (GO:0035264)\",\"BP: negative regulation of mammary gland epithelial cell proliferation (GO:0033600)\",\"BP: nucleotide-excision 