man_score\":49.66,\"human_quality\":\"gold\",\"human_fdr\":\"5.36e-5\",\"mouse_score\":59.29,\"mouse_quality\":\"gold\",\"mouse_fdr\":\"2.85e-4\"},{\"tissue_id\":\"UBERON:0001876\",\"tissue_name\":\"amygdala\",\"human_score\":52.11,\"human_quality\":\"gold\",\"human_fdr\":\"1.12e-5\",\"mouse_score\":52.72,\"mouse_quality\":\"silver\",\"mouse_fdr\":\"0.019\"},{\"tissue_id\":\"UBERON:0001954\",\"tissue_name\":\"Ammon\'s horn\",\"human_score\":45.9,\"human_quality\":\"gold\",\"human_fdr\":\"8.30e-4\",\"mouse_score\":57.66,\"mouse_quality\":\"gold\",\"mouse_fdr\":\"3.61e-5\"}]',0.6578947368421053,0.74),('development',3,'TP53',7157,'TP53',22059,'Trp53','ortholog_found','reviewed_found','reviewed_found','retrieved','retrieved','annotation_overlap_only','comparable',NULL,'[\"P04637\"]','[\"Cellular tumor antigen p53\"]','[\"1: Evidence at protein level\"]','[\"Multifunctional transcription factor that induces cell cycle arrest, DNA repair or apoptosis upon binding to its target DNA sequence (PubMed:11025664, PubMed:12524540, PubMed:12810724, PubMed:15186775, PubMed:15340061, PubMed:17317671, PubMed:17349958, PubMed:19556538, PubMed:20673990, PubMed:20959462, PubMed:22726440, PubMed:24051492, PubMed:24652652, PubMed:35618207, PubMed:36634798, PubMed:38653238, PubMed:9840937). Acts as a tumor suppressor in many tumor types; induces growth arrest or apoptosis depending on the physiological circumstances and cell type (PubMed:11025664, PubMed:12524540, PubMed:12810724, PubMed:15186775, PubMed:15340061, PubMed:17189187, PubMed:17317671, PubMed:17349958, PubMed:19556538, PubMed:20673990, PubMed:20959462, PubMed:22726440, PubMed:24051492, PubMed:24652652, PubMed:38653238, PubMed:9840937). Negatively regulates cell division by controlling expression of a set of genes required for this process (PubMed:11025664, PubMed:12524540, PubMed:12810724, PubMed:15186775, PubMed:15340061, PubMed:17317671, PubMed:17349958, PubMed:19556538, PubMed:20673990, PubMed:20959462, PubMed:22726440, PubMed:24051492, PubMed:24652652, PubMed:9840937). One of the activated genes is an inhibitor of cyclin-dependent kinases. Apoptosis induction seems to be mediated either by stimulation of BAX and FAS antigen expression, or by repression of Bcl-2 expression (PubMed:12524540, PubMed:17189187). Its pro-apoptotic activity is activated via its interaction with PPP1R13B/ASPP1 or TP53BP2/ASPP2 (PubMed:12524540). However, this activity is inhibited when the interaction with PPP1R13B/ASPP1 or TP53BP2/ASPP2 is displaced by PPP1R13L/iASPP (PubMed:12524540). In cooperation with mitochondrial PPIF is involved in activating oxidative stress-induced necrosis; the function is largely independent of transcription. Induces the transcription of long intergenic non-coding RNA p21 (lincRNA-p21) and lincRNA-Mkln1. LincRNA-p21 participates in TP53-dependent transcriptional repression leading to apoptosis and seems to have an effect on cell-cycle regulation. Implicated in Notch signaling cross-over. Prevents CDK7 kinase activity when associated to CAK complex in response to DNA damage, thus stopping cell cycle progression. Isoform 2 enhances the transactivation activity of isoform 1 from some but not all TP53-inducible promoters. Isoform 4 suppresses transactivation activity and impairs growth suppression mediated by isoform 1. Isoform 7 inhibits isoform 1-mediated apoptosis. Regulates the circadian clock by repressing CLOCK-BMAL1-mediated transcriptional activation of PER2 (PubMed:24051492)\"]','[\"Cytoplasm\",\"Cytoplasm, cytoskeleton, microtubule organizing center, centrosome\",\"Endoplasmic reticulum\",\"Mitochondrion matrix\",\"Nucleus\",\"Nucleus, PML body\"]','[\"MF: 14-3-3 protein binding (GO:0071889)\",\"MF: ATP-dependent DNA/DNA annealing activity (GO:0036310)\",\"MF: DNA binding (GO:0003677)\",\"MF: DNA-binding transcription activator activity, RNA polymerase II-specific (GO:0001228)\",\"MF: DNA-binding transcription factor activity (GO:0003700)\",\"MF: DNA-binding transcription f