N:0001882\",\"tissue_name\":\"nucleus accumbens\",\"human_score\":74.23,\"human_quality\":\"gold\",\"human_fdr\":\"1.07e-12\",\"mouse_score\":40.16,\"mouse_quality\":\"silver\",\"mouse_fdr\":\"0.036\"},{\"tissue_id\":\"UBERON:0002436\",\"tissue_name\":\"primary visual cortex\",\"human_score\":61.52,\"human_quality\":\"gold\",\"human_fdr\":\"9.13e-11\",\"mouse_score\":49.06,\"mouse_quality\":\"silver\",\"mouse_fdr\":\"0.028\"},{\"tissue_id\":\"UBERON:0005200\",\"tissue_name\":\"thoracic mammary gland\",\"human_score\":48.62,\"human_quality\":\"gold\",\"human_fdr\":\"1.87e-10\",\"mouse_score\":58.74,\"mouse_quality\":\"silver\",\"mouse_fdr\":\"0.015\"},{\"tissue_id\":\"UBERON:0002661\",\"tissue_name\":\"superior frontal gyrus\",\"human_score\":48.43,\"human_quality\":\"gold\",\"human_fdr\":\"4.47e-9\",\"mouse_score\":48.71,\"mouse_quality\":\"silver\",\"mouse_fdr\":\"0.035\"}]',0.43478260869565216,0.6285714285714286),('development',8,'ACE2',59272,'ACE2',70008,'Ace2','ortholog_found','reviewed_found','reviewed_found','retrieved','retrieved','annotation_overlap_only','comparable',NULL,'[\"Q9BYF1\"]','[\"Angiotensin-converting enzyme 2\"]','[\"1: Evidence at protein level\"]','[\"Essential counter-regulatory carboxypeptidase of the renin-angiotensin hormone system that is a critical regulator of blood volume, systemic vascular resistance, and thus cardiovascular homeostasis (PubMed:27217402). Converts angiotensin I to angiotensin 1-9, a nine-amino acid peptide with anti-hypertrophic effects in cardiomyocytes, and angiotensin II to angiotensin 1-7, which then acts as a beneficial vasodilator and anti-proliferation agent, counterbalancing the actions of the vasoconstrictor angiotensin II (PubMed:10924499, PubMed:10969042, PubMed:11815627, PubMed:14504186, PubMed:19021774). Also removes the C-terminal residue from three other vasoactive peptides, neurotensin, kinetensin, and des-Arg bradykinin, but is not active on bradykinin (PubMed:10969042, PubMed:11815627). Also cleaves other biological peptides, such as apelins (apelin-13, [Pyr1]apelin-13, apelin-17, apelin-36), casomorphins (beta-casomorphin-7, neocasomorphin) and dynorphin A with high efficiency (PubMed:11815627, PubMed:27217402, PubMed:28293165). In addition, ACE2 C-terminus is homologous to collectrin and is responsible for the trafficking of the neutral amino acid transporter SL6A19 to the plasma membrane of gut epithelial cells via direct interaction, regulating its expression on the cell surface and its catalytic activity (PubMed:18424768, PubMed:19185582) (Microbial infection) Acts as a receptor for human coronaviruses SARS-CoV and SARS-CoV-2, as well as human coronavirus NL63/HCoV-NL63 Non-functional as a carboxypeptidase (Microbial infection) Non-functional as a receptor for human coronavirus SARS-CoV-2\"]','[\"Apical cell membrane\",\"Cell membrane\",\"Cell projection, cilium\",\"Cytoplasm\",\"Secreted\"]','[\"MF: carboxypeptidase activity (GO:0004180)\",\"MF: endopeptidase activity (GO:0004175)\",\"MF: identical protein binding (GO:0042802)\",\"MF: metallopeptidase activity (GO:0008237)\",\"MF: peptidyl-dipeptidase activity (GO:0008241)\",\"MF: transporter activator activity (GO:0141109)\",\"MF: virus receptor activity (GO:0001618)\",\"MF: zinc ion binding (GO:0008270)\",\"BP: amino acid import across plasma membrane (GO:0089718)\",\"BP: angiotensin maturation (GO:0002003)\",\"BP: angiotensin-mediated drinking behavior (GO:0003051)\",\"BP: blood vessel diameter maintenance (GO:0097746)\",\"BP: entry receptor-mediated virion attachment to host cell (GO:0098670)\",\"BP: maternal process involved in female pregnancy (GO:0060135)\",\"BP: membrane fusion (GO:0061025)\",\"BP: negative regulation of ERK1 and ERK2 cascade (GO:0070373)\",\"BP: negative regulation of smooth muscle cell proliferation (GO:0048662)\",\"BP: negative regulation of transcription by RNA polymerase II (GO:0000122)\",\"BP: positive regulation of L-proline import across plasma membrane (GO:1905737)\",\"BP: positive regulation of amino acid transport (GO:0051957)\",\"BP: positive regulation of cardiac muscle contraction (GO:0060452)\",\"BP: positive regulation of gap junction assembly (GO:1903598)\",\"BP: positive regulation of reactive oxygen species metabolic process (GO:2000379)\",\"BP: receptor-mediated endocytosis of virus by host cell (GO:0019065)\",\"BP: receptor-mediated virion attachment to host cell (GO:0046813)\",\"BP: regulation of cardiac conduction (GO:1903779)\",\"BP: regulation of cell population proliferation (GO:0042127)\",\"BP: regulation of cytokine production (GO:0001817)\",\"BP: regulation of inflammatory response (GO:0050727)\",\"BP: regulation of systemic arterial blood pressure by renin-angiotensin (GO:0003081)\",\"BP: regulation of vasoconstriction (GO:0019229)\",\"BP: symbiont entry into host cell (GO:0046718)\",\"BP: tryptophan transport (GO:0015827)\",\"BP: viral life cycle (GO:0019058)\",\"CC: apical plasma membrane (GO:0016324)\",\"CC: brush border membrane (GO:0031526)\",\"CC: cell surface (GO:0009986)\",\"CC: cilium (GO:0005929)\",\"CC: cytoplasm (GO:0005737)\",\"CC: endocytic vesicle membrane (GO:0030666)\",\"CC: endoplasmic reticulum lumen (GO:0005788)\",\"CC: extracellular exosome (GO:0070062)\",\"CC: extracellular region (GO:0005576)\",\"CC: membrane (GO:0016020)\",\"CC: membrane raft (GO:0045121)\",\"CC: plasma membrane (GO:0005886)\",\"CC: transmembrane transporter complex (GO:1902495)\"]','[\"Q8R0I0\"]','[\"Angiotensin-converting enzyme 2\"]','[\"1: Evidence at protein level\"]','[\"Essential counter-regulatory carboxypeptidase of the renin-angiotensin hormone system that is a critical regulator of blood volume, systemic vascular resistance, and thus cardiovascular homeostasis. Converts angiotensin I to angiotensin 1-9, a nine-amino acid peptide with anti-hypertrophic effects in cardiomyocytes, and angiotensin II to angiotensin 1-7, which then acts as a beneficial vasodilator and anti-proliferation agent, counterbalancing the actions of the vasoconstrictor angiotensin II. Also removes the C-terminal residue from three other vasoactive peptides, neurotensin, kinetensin, and des-Arg bradykinin, but is not active on bradykinin. Also cleaves other biological peptides, such as apelins, casomorphins and dynorphin A (By similarity). By cleavage of angiotensin II, may be an important regulator of heart function (PubMed:12075344, PubMed:12967627). By cleavage of angiotensin II, may also have a protective role in acute lung injury (PubMed:16001071). Plays an important role in amino acid transport by acting as binding partner of amino acid transporter SLC6A19, regulating its trafficking on the cell surface and its activity (PubMed:18424768, PubMed:19185582, PubMed:22677001)\"]','[\"Apical cell membrane\",\"Cell membrane\",\"Cell projection, cilium\",\"Cytoplasm\",\"Secreted\"]','[\"MF: carboxypeptidase activity (GO:0004180)\",\"MF: endopeptidase activity (GO:0004175)\",\"MF: identical protein binding (GO:0042802)\",\"MF: metallocarboxypeptidase activity (GO:0004181)\",\"MF: metallopeptidase activity (GO:0008237)\",\"MF: peptidyl-dipeptidase activity (GO:0008241)\",\"MF: transporter activator activity (GO:0141109)\",\"MF: virus receptor activity (GO:0001618)\",\"BP: amino acid import across plasma membrane (GO:0089718)\",\"BP: angiotensin maturation (GO:0002003)\",\"BP: angiotensin-mediated drinking behavior (GO:0003051)\",\"BP: ceramide biosynthetic process (GO:0046513)\",\"BP: entry receptor-mediated virion attachment to host cell (GO:0098670)\",\"BP: maternal process involved in female pregnancy (GO:0060135)\",\"BP: negative regulation of ERK1 and ERK2 cascade (GO:0070373)\",\"BP: negative regulation of smooth muscle cell proliferation (GO:0048662)\",\"BP: negative regulation of transcription by RNA polymerase II (GO:0000122)\",\"BP: positive regulation of L-proline import across plasma membrane (GO:1905737)\",\"BP: positive regulation of amino acid transport (GO:0051957)\",\"BP: positive regulat