 pathway (PubMed:16284179, PubMed:33495445, PubMed:3883195, PubMed:6392892, PubMed:9435233). The TNF signaling pathway acts as a master regulator of the immune system, which either (1) promotes cell survival and inflammation by activating the canonical NF-kappa-B pathway or (2) trigger programmed cell death (apoptosis and necroptosis) (PubMed:16284179). Impairs regulatory T-cells (Treg) function in individuals with rheumatoid arthritis via FOXP3 dephosphorylation: acts by up-regulating the expression of protein phosphatase 1 (PP1), which dephosphorylates the key \'Ser-418\' residue of FOXP3, thereby inactivating FOXP3 and rendering Treg cells functionally defective (PubMed:23396208). Key mediator of cell death in the anticancer action of BCG-stimulated neutrophils in combination with DIABLO/SMAC mimetic in the RT4v6 bladder cancer cell line (PubMed:16829952, PubMed:22517918, PubMed:23396208). Induces insulin resistance in adipocytes via inhibition of insulin-induced IRS1 tyrosine phosphorylation and insulin-induced glucose uptake (By similarity). Induces GKAP42 protein degradation in adipocytes which is partially responsible for TNF-induced insulin resistance (By similarity). Plays a role in angiogenesis by inducing VEGF production synergistically with IL1B and IL6 (PubMed:12794819). Promotes osteoclastogenesis and therefore mediates bone resorption (By similarity) Cytokine mainly secreted by macrophages that binds to TNFRSF1A/TNFR1 and TNFRSF1B/TNFBR, activating the tumor necrosis factor-mediated (TNF) signaling pathway (PubMed:11592999, PubMed:16284179, PubMed:33495445, PubMed:3883195, PubMed:6392892). The TNF signaling pathway acts as a master regulator of the immune system, which either (1) promotes cell survival and inflammation by activating the canonical NF-kappa-B pathway or (2) trigger programmed cell death (apoptosis and necroptosis) (PubMed:16284179) The TNF intracellular domain (ICD) form induces IL12 production in dendritic cells The TNF intracellular domain (ICD) form induces IL12 production in dendritic cells\"]','[\"Cell membrane\",\"Membrane\",\"Secreted\"]','[\"MF: cytokine activity (GO:0005125)\",\"MF: histone H3K9ac reader activity (GO:0140072)\",\"MF: identical protein binding (GO:0042802)\",\"MF: protease binding (GO:0002020)\",\"MF: transcription cis-regulatory region binding (GO:0000976)\",\"MF: tumor necrosis factor receptor binding (GO:0005164)\",\"BP: antiviral innate immune response (GO:0140374)\",\"BP: astrocyte activation (GO:0048143)\",\"BP: calcium-mediated signaling (GO:0019722)\",\"BP: cell surface receptor signaling pathway via JAK-STAT (GO:0007259)\",\"BP: cellular response to amyloid-beta (GO:1904646)\",\"BP: cellular response to ionizing radiation (GO:0071479)\",\"BP: cellular response to nicotine (GO:0071316)\",\"BP: cellular response to retinoic acid (GO:0071300)\",\"BP: cellular response to toxic substance (GO:0097237)\",\"BP: cellular response to type II interferon (GO:0071346)\",\"BP: chronic inflammatory response to antigenic stimulus (GO:0002439)\",\"BP: circadian rhythm (GO:0007623)\",\"BP: cognition (GO:0050890)\",\"BP: detection of mechanical stimulus involved in sensory perception of pain (GO:0050966)\",\"BP: embryonic digestive tract development (GO:0048566)\",\"BP: endothelial cell apoptotic process (GO:0072577)\",\"BP: extrinsic apoptotic signaling pathway (GO:0097191)\",\"BP: extrinsic apoptotic signaling pathway via death domain receptors (GO:0008625)\",\"BP: immune response (GO:0006955)\",\"BP: inflammatory response (GO:0006954)\",\"BP: inflammatory response to wounding (GO:0090594)\",\"BP: leukocyte tethering or rolling (GO:0050901)\",\"BP: lipopolysaccharide-mediated signaling pathway (GO:0031663)\",\"BP: liver regeneration (GO:0097421)\",\"BP: macrophage activation involved in immune response (GO:0002281)\",\"BP: microglial cell activation (GO:0001774)\",\"BP: necroptotic signaling pathway (GO:0097527)\",\"BP: negative regulation of D-glucose import across plasma membra