O:0033209)\",\"BP: vascular endothelial growth factor production (GO:0010573)\",\"BP: vasodilation (GO:0042311)\",\"CC: cell surface (GO:0009986)\",\"CC: external side of plasma membrane (GO:0009897)\",\"CC: extracellular region (GO:0005576)\",\"CC: membrane raft (GO:0045121)\",\"CC: neuronal cell body (GO:0043025)\",\"CC: phagocytic cup (GO:0001891)\",\"CC: plasma membrane (GO:0005886)\",\"CC: recycling endosome (GO:0055037)\"]','[\"P06804\"]','[\"Tumor necrosis factor\"]','[\"1: Evidence at protein level\"]','[\"Cytokine that binds to TNFRSF1A/TNFR1 and TNFRSF1B/TNFBR, activating the tumor necrosis factor-mediated (TNF) signaling pathway (PubMed:33495441, PubMed:8395024). The TNF signaling pathway acts as a master regulator of the immune system, which either (1) promotes cell survival and inflammation by activating the canonical NF-kappa-B pathway or (2) trigger programmed cell death (apoptosis and necroptosis) (By similarity). Impairs regulatory T-cells (Treg) function in individuals with rheumatoid arthritis via FOXP3 dephosphorylation: acts by up-regulating the expression of protein phosphatase 1 (PP1), which dephosphorylates the key \'Ser-418\' residue of FOXP3, thereby inactivating FOXP3 and rendering Treg cells functionally defective (By similarity). Key mediator of cell death in the anticancer action of BCG-stimulated neutrophils in combination with DIABLO/SMAC mimetic in the RT4v6 bladder cancer cell line (By similarity). Induces insulin resistance in adipocytes via inhibition of insulin-induced IRS1 tyrosine phosphorylation and insulin-induced glucose uptake (PubMed:25586176). Induces GKAP42 protein degradation in adipocytes which is partially responsible for TNF-induced insulin resistance (PubMed:25586176). Plays a role in angiogenesis by inducing VEGF production synergistically with IL1B and IL6 (By similarity). Promotes osteoclastogenesis and therefore mediates bone resorption (PubMed:32741026) Cytokine mainly secreted by macrophages that binds to TNFRSF1A/TNFR1 and TNFRSF1B/TNFBR, activating the tumor necrosis factor-mediated (TNF) signaling pathway (PubMed:33495441, PubMed:8395024). The TNF signaling pathway acts as a master regulator of the immune system, which either (1) promotes cell survival and inflammation by activating the canonical NF-kappa-B pathway or (2) trigger programmed cell death (apoptosis and necroptosis) (By similarity) The TNF intracellular domain (ICD) form induces IL12 production in dendritic cells The TNF intracellular domain (ICD) form induces IL12 production in dendritic cells\"]','[\"Cell membrane\",\"Membrane\",\"Secreted\"]','[\"MF: cytokine activity (GO:0005125)\",\"MF: death receptor agonist activity (GO:0038177)\",\"MF: histone H3K9ac reader activity (GO:0140072)\",\"MF: identical protein binding (GO:0042802)\",\"MF: protease binding (GO:0002020)\",\"MF: receptor ligand activity (GO:0048018)\",\"MF: transcription cis-regulatory region binding (GO:0000976)\",\"MF: tumor necrosis factor receptor binding (GO:0005164)\",\"BP: JNK cascade (GO:0007254)\",\"BP: animal organ morphogenesis (GO:0009887)\",\"BP: antiviral innate immune response (GO:0140374)\",\"BP: apoptotic signaling pathway (GO:0097190)\",\"BP: calcium-mediated signaling (GO:0019722)\",\"BP: cell surface receptor signaling pathway via JAK-STAT (GO:0007259)\",\"BP: cellular extravasation (GO:0045123)\",\"BP: cellular response to amino acid stimulus (GO:0071230)\",\"BP: cellular response to ionizing radiation (GO:0071479)\",\"BP: cellular response to lipopolysaccharide (GO:0071222)\",\"BP: cellular response to nicotine (GO:0071316)\",\"BP: cellular response to type II interferon (GO:0071346)\",\"BP: chronic inflammatory response to antigenic stimulus (GO:0002439)\",\"BP: defense response (GO:0006952)\",\"BP: defense response to Gram-positive bacterium (GO:0050830)\",\"BP: defense response to bacterium (GO:0042742)\",\"BP: detection of mechanical stimulus involved in sensory perception of pain (GO:0050966)\",\"BP: embryonic di