\"]','[\"Participates in the induction of key genes involved in the response to hypoxia and in the induction of angiogenesis such as HIF1A (PubMed:35455969). Involved in protecting cells from hypoxia-mediated cell death (By similarity) Growth factor active in angiogenesis, vasculogenesis and endothelial cell growth (PubMed:34530889). Induces endothelial cell proliferation, promotes cell migration, inhibits apoptosis and induces permeabilization of blood vessels. Binds to the FLT1/VEGFR1 and KDR/VEGFR2 receptors, heparan sulfate and heparin. Binds to the NRP1/neuropilin-1 receptor. Binding to NRP1 initiates a signaling pathway needed for motor neuron axon guidance and cell body migration, including for the caudal migration of facial motor neurons from rhombomere 4 to rhombomere 6 during embryonic development (By similarity). Also binds the DEAR/FBXW7-AS1 receptor (PubMed:17446437) Binds to the KDR receptor but does not activate downstream signaling pathways, does not activate angiogenesis and inhibits tumor growth\"]','[\"Cytoplasm\",\"Endoplasmic reticulum\",\"Golgi apparatus\",\"Nucleus\",\"Secreted\",\"Secreted, extracellular space, extracellular matrix\"]','[\"MF: chemoattractant activity (GO:0042056)\",\"MF: cytokine activity (GO:0005125)\",\"MF: extracellular matrix binding (GO:0050840)\",\"MF: fibronectin binding (GO:0001968)\",\"MF: growth factor activity (GO:0008083)\",\"MF: heparin binding (GO:0008201)\",\"MF: identical protein binding (GO:0042802)\",\"MF: neuropilin binding (GO:0038191)\",\"MF: platelet-derived growth factor receptor binding (GO:0005161)\",\"MF: receptor ligand activity (GO:0048018)\",\"MF: transmembrane receptor protein tyrosine kinase activator activity (GO:0030297)\",\"MF: vascular endothelial growth factor receptor 1 binding (GO:0043183)\",\"MF: vascular endothelial growth factor receptor 2 binding (GO:0043184)\",\"MF: vascular endothelial growth factor receptor binding (GO:0005172)\",\"BP: VEGF-activated neuropilin signaling pathway (